axpbox: axpbox (alpha emulator)
axpbox:
axpbox: AXPbox is a fork of the es40 emulator.
axpbox: It could theoretically be used for running any operating system that
axpbox: runs on the OpenVMS or Tru64 PALcode e.g. OpenVMS, Windows 2000,
axpbox: Tru64 UNIX, Linux, NetBSD,..
axpbox:
axpbox: The emulator supports SCSI, sound, IDE, serial ports, Ethernet
axpbox: using pcap, or TUN/TAP on Linux and VGA graphics (using SDL3).
